{
  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "Evidence: Two completed experiments (config_004, config_047) share all settings except image encoder (ResNet50 vs ViT-L). config_047 (ViT-L, pca_n2000, avgpool, concat) leads with 0.6287 acc at a surprisingly low 4.54 GPU-hr cost. The ~1% accuracy gap is suggestive but based on a single comparison, and F1 actually dropped slightly, so the evidence is still thin. Question: config_001 is identical to config_047 except it uses weighted fusion instead of concat, directly testing whether a learned fusion weighting can improve on the current best while keeping the same cheap architecture. Why this is the best next step: It is a minimal, low-cost exploitation of the most promising configuration (expected cost ~4–5 GPU hrs, similar to config_047), reduces uncertainty about the fusion strategy without introducing multiple confounding changes, and preserves budget for later experiments to explore RNA encoders (scgpt/scvi_n200) and transformer aggregation. If weighted fusion helps, we gain a stronger base; if not, we rule it out cheaply and can pivot to larger architectural changes in experiments 4–10."
}

